From b385ed41b05e66d02207e3d67349ddaa1dabb8bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cuadra8998 <cuadra8998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:40:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] accel: ordered frames on NMXGPU's panel (copied once the GPU
 has published them)

WindowServer waited for the GPU after every Metal flush on the panel
(commitAndWaitUntilSubmitted -> waitUntilCompleted) so the transaction's
copy found finished pixels: a frame cost its CPU encoding plus its GPU
time, the GPU idled half the time and its clock stayed at RPe. Launchpad
ran at 25-30 fps with 35-68 ms frames (sample of WindowServer, MeowXE3
1.0.13).

Now debug.nmxfb_blob_ordered (on by default for the panel) also covers
NMXIntelGPUFB: the plugin only waits for scheduling and numbers its
command buffers (NMXPending/NMXPublished, as for the VM display), and the
transaction hands the surface to a thread call that waits until the
command buffers committed before it are published, then copies the frame
once and flips it on (iopCopySurface/iopCopyTail, split out of
performTransactionCopy) and completes the transaction. The wait re-arms
every 250 us instead of sleeping in 1 ms steps, and is capped at 100 ms.
The front-buffer re-copy stays off.

Launchpad, 12 s: 38.2 fps instead of 26.4, gaps over 34 ms 65 instead of
179; the wait per frame averages 1.6 ms. Same kernel imports.
debug.nmxfb_blob_ordered=0 goes back to WindowServer waiting, live.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
